{"type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"api_error_status":null,"duration_ms":231434,"duration_api_ms":233155,"num_turns":1,"result":"## Project State Summary\n\n**Problem:** GNU coreutils have no formal specs accessible to implementers. This project derives formal specifications from C source, generates Go implementations via AI, and verifies parity through differential testing against Homebrew reference binaries.\n\n**Architecture:** Four-stage pipeline (extract → specify → synthesize → verify). Key components: `docs/specs/` (SRDs, use cases), `cmd/` (one package per utility), `pkg/` (shared sys/format/testutils libraries), `magefiles/` (build automation). Differential testing via `pkg/testutils` compares Go binaries against `g`-prefixed Homebrew GNU binaries.\n\n**Implementation state:** This is generation run 44. Many utilities are implemented; many still need code. The `requirement_states` field shows which SRDs have requirements in \"ready\" state, indicating they're queued for generation.\n\n**Current release focus:** Release 11.1 (users, who, pinky). The `users` utility (srd096) was just completed (see recent commits). The remaining use cases are `who` (srd097) and `pinky` (srd098), both with all requirements in \"ready\" state.\n\n## Priority Reasoning\n\nRelease 11.1 is the earliest incomplete release with \"ready\" requirements. The two remaining use cases are:\n- **srd097-who** (11 requirements: R1.1-R1.4, R2.1-R2.4, R3.1-R3.3)\n- **srd098-pinky** (9 requirements: R1.1-R1.3, R2.1-R2.3, R3.1-R3.3)\n\nBoth utilities read the utmpx database, so the just-completed `cmd/users` serves as a pattern reference. They are independent of each other (no cross-dependency).\n\nPer P8 (deterministic ordering by primary file path), `cmd/pinky` comes before `cmd/who` alphabetically.\n\n## Weight Budget Checks\n\nAssuming default weight=1 for all requirements (weight-4 requirements are restructured into their own groups per project convention):\n\n```\nTask 0: srd098 R1.1(w=1) + R1.2(w=1) + R1.3(w=1) = 3 ≤ 4 ✓\nTask 1: srd098 R2.1(w=1) + R2.2(w=1) + R2.3(w=1) = 3 ≤ 4 ✓\nTask 2: srd098 R3.1(w=1) + R3.2(w=1) + R3.3(w=1) = 3 ≤ 4 ✓\nTask 3: srd097 R1.1(w=1) + R1.2(w=1) + R1.3(w=1) + R1.4(w=1) = 4 ≤ 4 ✓\n```\n\nAll within budget. 4 tasks total (at limit). Covers all of pinky and starts who.\n\n```yaml\n- index: 0\n  title: \"[stitch] Implement cmd/pinky core functionality (srd098 R1.1, R1.2, R1.3)\"\n  dependency: -1\n  description: |\n    deliverable_type: code\n\n    required_reading:\n      - docs/specs/software-requirements/srd098-pinky.yaml (full SRD -- implements R1.1, R1.2, R1.3)\n      - cmd/users/main.go (utmpx reading pattern reference -- same release, same database)\n      - cmd/users/users_test.go (differential testing pattern reference)\n      - pkg/testutils/difftest.go (DiffTest struct and RunDiffTests function signatures)\n      - pkg/sys/sigpipe.go (InstallSIGPIPEHandler for SIGPIPE handling)\n\n    files:\n      - path: cmd/pinky/main.go\n        action: create\n        note: pinky utility -- core user lookup with GECOS field display via utmpx\n\n    requirements:\n      - id: R1\n        text: \"Implement srd098-pinky R1.1 as specified in the SRD\"\n      - id: R2\n        text: \"Implement srd098-pinky R1.2 as specified in the SRD\"\n      - id: R3\n        text: \"Implement srd098-pinky R1.3 as specified in the SRD\"\n\n    design_decisions:\n      - id: D1\n        text: \"Call sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler() at the start of main per project convention\"\n      - id: D2\n        text: \"Read utmpx database for login session data, following the same pattern used in cmd/users\"\n      - id: D3\n        text: \"Reference binary is gpinky from Homebrew GNU coreutils\"\n\n    acceptance_criteria:\n      - id: AC1\n        text: \"cmd/pinky/main.go compiles with go build -o bin/pinky ./cmd/pinky/\"\n      - id: AC2\n        text: \"go vet ./cmd/pinky/ passes with no warnings\"\n      - id: AC3\n        text: \"srd098 R1.1, R1.2, R1.3 are implemented as specified in the SRD\"\n\n- index: 1\n  title: \"[stitch] Implement cmd/pinky output formatting and flags (srd098 R2.1, R2.2, R2.3)\"\n  dependency: 0\n  description: |\n    deliverable_type: code\n\n    required_reading:\n      - docs/specs/software-requirements/srd098-pinky.yaml (full SRD -- implements R2.1, R2.2, R2.3)\n      - cmd/pinky/main.go (existing core implementation from prior task)\n\n    files:\n      - path: cmd/pinky/main.go\n        action: modify\n        note: Add output formatting modes, flag handling, and column display options\n\n    requirements:\n      - id: R1\n        text: \"Implement srd098-pinky R2.1 as specified in the SRD\"\n      - id: R2\n        text: \"Implement srd098-pinky R2.2 as specified in the SRD\"\n      - id: R3\n        text: \"Implement srd098-pinky R2.3 as specified in the SRD\"\n\n    design_decisions:\n      - id: D1\n        text: \"Follow GNU gpinky flag semantics exactly as specified in the SRD\"\n      - id: D2\n        text: \"Maintain compatibility with the core utmpx reading from the prior task\"\n\n    acceptance_criteria:\n      - id: AC1\n        text: \"cmd/pinky/main.go compiles with go build -o bin/pinky ./cmd/pinky/\"\n      - id: AC2\n        text: \"go vet ./cmd/pinky/ passes with no warnings\"\n      - id: AC3\n        text: \"srd098 R2.1, R2.2, R2.3 are implemented as specified in the SRD\"\n\n- index: 2\n  title: \"[stitch] Implement cmd/pinky error handling and differential tests (srd098 R3.1, R3.2, R3.3)\"\n  dependency: 1\n  description: |\n    deliverable_type: code\n\n    required_reading:\n      - docs/specs/software-requirements/srd098-pinky.yaml (full SRD -- implements R3.1, R3.2, R3.3)\n      - cmd/pinky/main.go (existing implementation from prior tasks)\n      - cmd/users/users_test.go (differential testing pattern -- same utmpx-based utility)\n      - pkg/testutils/difftest.go (DiffTest struct, RunDiffTests, BuildBinary)\n\n    files:\n      - path